  "body": "## Scope and dependency\n\nDepends on draft #407 at `78bdd4df465d1c7d8a752f9df0ed714ecad2330d`. Do not merge independently.\n\nAdds `POST /event-operations/events/{eventId}/tasks/{activityId}/complete`, strict Haskell types, transactional receipt decoding, OpenAPI and generated web declarations. Reuses canonical SQL task/RACI/dependency/revision/audit/receipt domains and the current session fence. No second system, new migration, manual client helper or UI control.\n\n## Requirements and invariants\n\nCA01\u201305 / EO-026\u2013028, EO-045/051, EO-052\u2013058: authenticated actor only; session revalidation, command and receipt validation in the same transaction; success only after COMMIT. Exact receipt binding to target/key, completed status, INTEGER range and expected+1 BIGINT revision. Invalid receipts throw before commit. Sanitized failures, current read authority for historical replay, private/no-store handler responses, no implicit retry/rebase or override.\n\n## Executed verification\n\nBefore implementation, the full pinned formal suite passed: 24 positive TLC configurations, 60 named negative controls, 13 PlusCal integrity tests, 2 SAT Alloy scenarios and 13 UNSAT assertions. Existing applicable models were reused unchanged; finite bounds and trusted SQL assumptions are documented, not universal proof claims.\n\n- `sh scripts/test-event-operations-http.sh`: final 107 examples, zero failures, including five 100-case properties. Real Stack/GHC 9.10.3 authentication/subrouter and disposable PG16. Tests include strict inputs, dependency/RACI/lifecycle guards, hidden targets, replay/concurrent retries, nine malformed post-write receipts, deferred COMMIT failure with verified rollback, post-authentication revocation, maximal BIGINT transport/replay, legacy overflow, disabled feature and absent SQL.\n- 32 runner/CI regression tests passed; both local/hosted HTTP harnesses install the prerequisite.\n- Regenerated web types with openapi-typescript 7.10.1; structured OpenAPI assertions passed.\n- Existing web API suite: 150 tests passed. Complete web typecheck passed without weakened compiler options.\n- `npm run quality:repo`: 147 tests, fixture verification and heuristic audit passed; the audit still reports 356 warnings/9,419 informational findings, not a model-checking proof.\n- Shell syntax and whitespace checks passed. Owned HTTP test containers were removed; no external database was targeted.\n\nNo new full application backend build, native mobile build/generation, browser E2E, accessibility or performance audit. SQL migrations are unchanged; #407 records the separate PG16 concurrency/down-up and PG17 authoritative complete-schema evidence. Hosted CI on this head remains unverified until it runs. Parent #407 has a failed catalog audit and pending backend/real-browser checks; no waiver or all-green claim.\n\n## Schema, privacy, rollback and manual steps\n\nNo production migration, manifest, feature flag, credentials or provider changed. The reduced HTTP fixture gains the existing real activity `updated_at` column, not a production schema change. Current scoped authority and safe hidden-target errors are preserved; the request body cannot supply actor/time/hash/grants/override.\n\nRemove/disable the route before rolling back the private SQL function. Missing SQL returns 503 without a legacy-write fallback. Preserve completed work, revisions, accepted keys, receipts and audit. Production activation still needs separately reviewed migration/flags/DB execution grants. No production rollout, merge or real-money action.\n\n## Remaining limitations\n\nTyped command helper and scoped completion review UX are next. Approvals/evidence, justified override, reopening, live-event effects, notifications, retention/removal, native mobile and durable offline queues remain separate work. After an ambiguous network result, retain the original body/key for authorized exact replay. The overall event-operations mission is not complete.\n\n[Contract, bounds, exact formal command and traceability](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/blob/feat/event-task-completion-api/docs/event-operations/task-completion-api-contract.md)\n\n[Full verification report and local-only example](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/blob/feat/event-task-completion-api/docs/event-operations/pr-32-task-completion-api.md)\n",
